                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okay so not sure if this Linux junk but the game only runs foregrounded and the time from game-over to playable was, like. A minute. And I died often so that kinda added up.\n\nAlright that's my only bitch, this game fuckin rocks. The JRPG combat is nice and deep and has its own jank and your strategy will likely evolve and deepen over the game. The story is absolutely wild. At first the NPCs say a bunch of ignorant shit and you're like \"damn the writing sucks\" and then ten hours in your partner says some shit about the hotel you're in and you're like \"wait that's why all those NPCs are fucked in the head\" and then all the little ideas and notes snap together like puzzle pieces forming the border of the scene, leaving the interior empty and alluring\n\nAmelia is not useless, she deserves good things. I am Diane's biggest fan",
